**Read:** [Graduate Logistics Systems — MIT ESD.260J](../sources/Graduate-Logistics-Systems-MIT.lingua#r_4NMCCS7JPNK6CD9V9Z4XTQPKR8), the complete cost/service and system-design work; [Graduate Supply Chain Planning — MIT 15.762J](../sources/Graduate-Supply-Chain-Planning-MIT.lingua#r_16MZ0PJM4KC10A3D9AYYESBT6P), the full integrated planning programme; [Enterprise-wide Optimization: A New Frontier in Process Systems Engineering — Grossmann](../sources/Enterprise-wide-Optimization-Grossmann.lingua#r_4XD1X5QN83H40RBMGJVSZY9Y8V), the complete objective/integration discussion; [Supply chain management for the process industry — Songsong Liu](../sources/Process-Industry-Supply-Chain-Management-Liu.lingua#r_5W74Q34MKEJAWVS30JV4QH01YQ), complete relevant multiobjective and capacity-planning chapters.

Choose two technically feasible supply arrangements and define a common delivered service. Include the material/active-content price, transport, equipment ownership, energy/water, contact components, analysis, inventory, trained work, maintenance, losses and recovery. Keep cash flow, physical resources, emissions and service consequences separately inspectable before combining objectives.

Use dated cost assumptions and compare sensitivity rather than presenting a historical handbook price as current. Account for minimum shipment/campaign, reserve readiness and qualification delays. A large installed source can have scale benefits while increasing dependence or forcing inventory that ages before use. A local source can avoid one transport leg but add conditioning or analytic work.

Develop a discounted life-cycle comparison only after stating the period, discount assumption, replacements, residual value and service boundary. Use the shared quantitative methods for the calculation. Compare robustness under changing demand, input quality and interruption duration. Distinguish an economic preference from a physical requirement or a distributional judgement about whose consequences count. The advanced integrated study should show alternatives and uncertainty, with enough detail that another reader can change the assumptions and reproduce the result.

**Continue:** [Trace chemical losses to their physical pathway and evidence](../recovery/Storage-and-transfer-losses-as-material-and-environmental-flows.lingua#r_341X99P6FEVRPYKJZNA5YA41X2).

